    "body": "## Summary\n\nFix incorrect draft query width in the FlashAttention backend when using DSpark speculative decoding with `sample_from_anchor=False`.\n\n## Root Cause\n\nThe FlashAttention backend called `resolve_num_tokens_per_req()` directly to compute the speculative verify width. This did not account for DSpark's `sample_from_anchor=False` case, where each request produces **gamma+1 rows** (one extra anchor row) instead of gamma rows. The resulting width mismatch caused incorrect draft query dimensions in FlashAttention v3/v4 backends.\n\n## Fix\n\nReplace the direct `resolve_num_tokens_per_req()` call with `model_runner.decode_num_tokens_per_req()`, which is the single source of truth for decode-time token counts and correctly handles all speculative algorithms including DSpark.\n\n**File changed:** `python/sglang/srt/layers/attention/flashattention_backend.py`\n\n## Testing\n\n- Verified that DSpark speculative decoding with FA3/FA4 backends produces correct output with `sample_from_anchor=False`.\n- Standard speculative decoding paths (non-DSpark) remain unaffected since `decode_num_tokens_per_req()` returns the same value as before for those cases.\n\nCloses #46476\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #40259035880](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/40259035880)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #40259035891](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/40259035891)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #40259035810](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/40259035810)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
